| Simone Todaro | 113 | ~3% |
| peter279k | 91 | ~3% |
| Tomasz Wrona | 61 | ~2% |

**Who is still around:** In the last 12 months, `src/` and `tests/` got commits from Tomasz Wrona (3), Ben Ramsey (2), Kasia Nowak (1) and github-actions (1). The other big contributors have no commits in `src/` or `tests/` in that window.

**If Ben leaves**
- You lose the author of over half of both directories, and the only active person who knows most of the original design.
- Tomasz is the only plausible successor. He has about 10% of `src/`, and he is the sole author of the newest code in `tests/Support/`, which holds the chunk, value-extractor and value-to-string trait tests. That area is a bus factor of 1 on its own.
- The script fell back to Ben as the repo-wide owner (`*`). Once he's gone, nothing in `CODEOWNERS` names a replacement.
- Carlos, icanhazstring, zf2timo and Kévin together wrote a large share of the code, but their recent activity is nil, so they can't be treated as reviewers. I didn't check whether they're still reachable outside the repo.

**Caveats**
- Line counts measure who wrote the code, not who understands it. A reviewer who never commits looks like a stranger here.
- Rename and move handling in blame is good but not perfect.
- I didn't check whether the activity window fits Kasia Nowak, who has a single commit.

If you want, I can write the `CODEOWNERS` and a fuller risk report. The script would put `.github/CODEOWNERS` and `ownership.json` into the repo, so I'm leaving those files alone until you say so.

