FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Ben Ramsey wrote most of the code. Counting by lines, they wrote about 61% of `src/` and 55% of `tests/`. The most likely thing you'd lose without them is knowledge of the core design. Everyone else has written much less.

I used `git blame -w -M -C` on the files as they stand today, with `.mailmap` applied. That gives the lines each person last wrote, not their commit counts.

## `src/` (about 3,550 lines)

| Author | Lines | Share | What they own |
|---|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 2,171 | ~61% | `AbstractArray`, `AbstractCollection`, `Collection`, all the interfaces except the queue ones, `AbstractMap`, `NamedParameterMap`, `Grouping`, `Sort`, `TypeTrait`, `ValueExtractorTrait`, most exceptions |
| Tomasz Wrona | 358 | ~10% | See the caveat below. 295 lines are one generated file and 51 are `ChunkTrait`. |
| Carlos C Soto | 270 | ~8% | `Set`, `AbstractSet`, `TypedMap`, `AbstractTypedMap`, `ValueToStringTrait` |
| zf2timo | 223 | ~6% | `Queue`, the queue exceptions |
| icanhazstring | 199 | ~6% | Spread across several files, with no file mostly theirs |
| Kévin Gomez | 145 | ~4% | `DoubleEndedQueue` |
| Everyone else | under 30 each | ~5% | One-off fixes |

## `tests/` (about 3,640 lines)

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Ben Ramsey | 1,964 | ~54% |
| icanhazstring | 594 | ~16% |
| Kévin Gomez | 329 | ~9% |
| Carlos C Soto | 204 | ~6% |
| zf2timo | 174 | ~5% |
| Simone Todaro | 113 | ~3% |
| peter279k | 91 | ~2.5% |
| Tomasz Wrona | 61 | ~2% |

icanhazstring is the clear number two on tests. Most of the other authors' test lines are in their own areas: queue tests for Kévin Gomez, set and typed-map tests for Carlos C Soto.

## Caveats

- **Tomasz Wrona's 10% in `src/` is misleading.** Of their 358 lines, 295 are `src/Generated/TypeMap.php`. Its header says `@generated by bin/generate-types.php, do not edit by hand`, but `bin/` isn't in the repo and nothing else references the file. So the generator is missing or was never committed, and nobody can regenerate the file. Hand-written work from them is just `ChunkTrait` (51 lines), plus a 20-line mechanical namespace rename (`Tool` to `Support`) that I didn't count as authorship. Find out where that generator lives before the handover.
- **Not everything can be attributed to a real person.** There are 12 `github-actions[bot]` lines in `src/`. The author "Kasia Nowak" (2 lines in `src/`) uses an `@nowak.example` address, and Tomasz Wrona's address is on a `.example` domain. Check that those identities are real before you list them as contacts. `.mailmap` already merges `T. Wrona` into `Tomasz Wrona`.
- **Line counts aren't design knowledge.** Blame won't show who understands the architecture. I only counted authorship, not who reviewed or maintained things.

## If Ben Ramsey left

- **The core library would lose its one deep owner.** Ben wrote nearly every file that defines the public API: the base classes, the collection, map and array interfaces, grouping and sorting. Nobody else has authored more than ~8% of `src/`. They also wrote over half the tests, which are the safety net for changing any of that.
- **Some areas have a second owner:**
  - Queues: zf2timo and Kévin Gomez.
  - Sets and typed maps: Carlos C Soto.
  - Test breadth: icanhazstring.
- **Some areas have no backup:**
  - The abstract base classes.
  - The interfaces.
  - `Grouping`, `Sort` and the map implementations.
  - The generated type map, which has no generator and no maintainer.

Before handover I'd do two things. Pair Ben with someone on the core classes, and find or rewrite `bin/generate-types.php`. Carlos C Soto and icanhazstring are the best candidates to ask. I can also break this down by file or run a bus-factor report if you want it.

