## If Ben Ramsey left

- **Bus factor:** Ben alone holds more than 50% of the lines in both directories (bus factor 1, counted on surviving lines). Reaching 80% takes 3 authors in each. Counting blank lines in tests/, reaching 80% takes 4 authors.
- **Active people:** only 3 of 16 src/ authors and 2 of 13 tests/ authors have committed in the last 365 days (as of 2026-09-01). In src/ the active people are Ben, Tomasz Wrona and one other. In tests/ they are Ben and Tomasz Wrona. Ben is the only active bus-factor-1 holder in both. 27.8% of src/ lines and 43.0% of tests/ lines belong to people with no commit in that window.
- **src/ without Ben:** he holds 1,961 of 2,798 lines (70.1%) and is the top owner of 20 of 32 files. Nine files (758 lines) would have nobody who knows them, meaning the remaining authors each hold under 10% of them. They include:
  - `AbstractMap.php`: Ben's code is 98.3% of it.
  - `AbstractArray.php`
  - `Map/MapInterface.php`
  - `Map/NamedParameterMap.php`
  - `Grouping.php`
  - `Support/TypeTrait.php`
  - `GenericArray.php`: 100% Ben.
- **tests/ without Ben:** he holds 1,557 of 2,819 lines (55.2%) and is the top owner of 24 of 32 files. Fifteen files (632 lines) would have nobody who knows them. Several are 100% Ben's, with no one else holding any lines:
  - `tests/types/*.php`
  - `GroupingTest.php`
  - `TypesTest.php`
- **Likely inheritors:**
  - In src/: Carlos C Soto (238 lines in 12 files), zf2timo (196 lines in 16 files) and icanhazstring (149 lines in 8 files). All three have been inactive for years.
  - In tests/: icanhazstring (460 lines in 12 files), Kévin Gomez (212 lines in 2 files) and zf2timo (118 lines in 3 files).
  - Tomasz Wrona is the only other recently active author, and holds only 2% of each directory.

This counts lines, not understanding. It says nothing about review, design or mentoring.

## What the numbers include and leave out

- **Identity merge:** `.mailmap` already merges `<email redacted>` into Ben Ramsey (110 lines in src/, 94 in tests/). Those lines are in his figures above. The `.mailmap` also maps T. Wrona to Tomasz Wrona.
- **Bots:** `github-actions[bot]` is excluded (12 lines, 1 commit) and gets no credit.
- **Generated code:** `src/Generated/TypeMap.php` (295 lines) is left out of every number.
- **Credited to the original author, not the committer:**
  - Ben committed 20 lines that are credited to Raphael Tomé Santana. They come from the revert 19effc8.
  - Ben committed 8 lines in src/ and 18 in tests/ that are credited to Mohamed Younes (77a182e).
  - Ben committed 81 lines in tests/ that are credited to peter279k (bf292fb).
  - GitHub committed 16 test lines credited to Tom Carrio (1c1d5f9) and 30 credited to Ben (4a02cef).
- **Mechanical commits:** the tool checked for mechanical rewrites and set none aside. It flagged two as looking mechanical and left them in:
  - 3b40daf, "Apply php-cs-fixer changes", by `github-actions[bot]`, with 12 surviving lines.
  - c3611fa, "Rename Tool namespace to Support", by Tomasz Wrona, with 12 surviving lines in src/ and 8 in tests/.
- **Copy detection:** this affects Ben's figures. In src/ he holds 70.1% with copy detection and 73.5% without. In tests/ it is 55.2% with and 63.3% without. Lines that moved or were copied go to other authors, mainly zf2timo and Kévin Gomez, so the with-copy figures are the ones above.
- **Workflow:** 15% of commits are merges. Lines go to the authors of the merged branches, not to whoever merged.

